  "data_abstract": "CERN-LHC.\r\nA set of jet shapes for a small resolution parameter $R = 0.2$ was\r\nmeasured at mid-rapidity for $0$-$10\\%$ central Pb-Pb collisions at a centre-of-mass energy $\\sqrt{\\rm{s_{NN}}}$=2.76 TeV with the ALICE detector at the Large Hadron Collider (LHC).\r\nThis set of jet shapes includes the first radial moment or angularity, $g$; the momentum dispersion,\r\n $p_{\\rm T}D$; and the difference between the leading and sub-leading\r\n constituent track transverse momentum, $LeSub$. These observables provide complementary information on the\r\n jet fragmentation and can constrain different aspects of the theoretical description of jet-medium interactions.\r\n The measured jet shapes are compared with PYTHIA calculations.",
  "data_keywords": {
    "cmenergies": [
      {
        "gte": 7000.0,
        "lte": 7000.0
      },
      {
        "gte": 2760.0,
        "lte": 7000.0
      }
    ],
    "reactions": [
      "RE: p p --> jet + X",
      "RE: PB PB --> jet + X"
    ]
  },
